nsor data determined by the temperature sensors 52, the control sub-system 54 may determine fluid temperature at multiple different locations along the bore in the pipeline system 10 (process block 106)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11199502-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is very easy to produce the natural gas hydrate in the oil and gas exploitation and transportation process especially in low-temperature and high-pressure deep water environments, and the natural gas hydrate will block a conveying pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if, at block 7069, the system 6000 is currently in a normal water production mode, the target temperature 7068 along with a product or condensate output temperature 7070 determined from data provided by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as shown, in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if, in block 8016, the system 6000 is not in a production start-up state, in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, at block 7069, the system 6000 is currently in a normal water production mode, the target temperature 7068 along with a product or condensate output temperature 7070 determined from data provided by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "as shown, in block 6592 a controller may determine a difference between a desired temperature and the source inlet temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, in block 8016, the system 6000 is not in a production start-up state, in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-11559765-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "at block 720, the controller 180 may determine a dew point of the chamber 28 and an optimal post-evaporator air temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11623178-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "at block 720, the controller 180 may determine a dew point of the chamber 28 and an optimal post-evaporator air temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-5776333-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "US-5858248-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "US-7723700-B2", "para_id": "para_19", "text": "via the ion source block, the surfaces of conduit 150 are thus preferably maintained at temperature greater than the set-point of pid 3"}, {"pat_id": "US-9370746-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when a pressure pump that delivers supply water to the ro membrane module is operated at a constant operating pressure, a water volume of produced permeate water (pure water) becomes mailer than a required production volume of water, when a temperature of supply water is low or when a membrane is blocked"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "it is noted that changes of the temperature of a compressible gas in the modified inlet block 444 may cause the gas to expand or contract, and thereby result in unwanted variances in the flow rate"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "to avoid such unwanted fluctuations in temperature, the increased surface area, or contact area of the chambers 447 provides a heat exchanger interface between the fluid and the material that forms the modified inlet block 444 and thereby minimize changes in fluid temperature as the fluid moves along the surface of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "to avoid such unwanted fluctuations in temperature, the increased surface area, or contact area of the chambers 447 provides a heat exchanger interface between the fluid and the material that forms the modified inlet block 444 and thereby minimize changes in fluid temperature as the fluid moves along the surface of the modified inlet block 444"}]</data>
