  <data key="d5">["conduit", "example", "room", "tank", "heating", "wave", "step", "controller", "level", "delivery", "difference", "signal", "moisture", "main", "air", "check", "minute", "sensor", "result", "point", "presence", "system", "defense", "reading", "consumer", "user", "tolerance", "set", "property", "testing", "floor", "time", "area", "control", "quality", "past", "embodiment", "increase", "repair", "threshold", "manifold", "coil", "way", "peak", "equipment", "condensate", "blockage", "apparati", "exchanger", "entrance", "configuration", "detector", "box", "limit", "degree", "touch", "drive", "accuracy", "fuel", "module", "value", "feedline", "leak", "change", "range", "source", "rate", "temperature", "heater", "heat", "wait", "freeze", "take", "toilet", "site", "flow", "fig", "replacement", "arrangement", "pressure", "lng", "communication", "leakage", "tap", "relationship", "work", "addition", "shift", "line", "end", "positioning", "art", "baseline", "assembly", "detection", "density", "mode", "order", "water", "calculation", "drain", "effect", "exhaust", "pipeline", "method", "engine", "generating", "determination", "device", "condition", "side", "period", "error", "pipe", "state", "invention", "drop", "plurality", "variance", "test", "location", "distribution", "meter", "valve", "fixture", "damage"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["include", "generate", "consume", "allow", "cause", "access", "connect", "represent", "condense", "provide", "have", "check", "try", "assume", "note", "be", "illustrate", "get", "turn on", "show", "lead", "control", "steam", "contain", "increase", "prevent", "mark", "associate", "utilize", "discuss", "compromise", "mimic", "make", "sense", "drive", "compensate", "fail", "go", "fall", "leak", "change", "position", "produce", "surround", "reach", "localize", "incorporate", "flow", "begin", "determine", "equip", "perform", "configure", "detect", "end", "know", "build up", "indicate", "match", "occur", "say", "base", "mean", "compare", "use", "drain", "locate", "pipeline", "leak out", "enter", "maintain", "convey", "exit", "stop", "open up", "cool", "exceed"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c (one f to three f) between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode, the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, only differences between the exhaust assembly 30 and the exhaust assembly 330 are specifically noted herein, such as differences in the positioning of the temperature sensors, and how the control system determines a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "10, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase (i.e., positive rate of change) again to a second peak or leakage temperature limit 690a after the water heater enters the standby mode from the heating mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after (e.g., about two minutes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, the first temperature sensor 414 may be detecting a temperature of the residual condensate produced during the heating mode that has already begun to cool to a lower temperature (i.e., temperature lower than the leaking water) within the drain line 394"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, the first temperature sensor 414 may be detecting a temperature of the residual condensate produced during the heating mode that has already begun to cool to a lower temperature (i.e., temperature lower than the leaking water) within the drain line 394"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9-11, only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "further, since any slight increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 at the end of the wait period 695 might indicate that there is a leak, the controller may be able to detect even smaller leaks"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9 represents another way that the temperature sensors may be positioned in a condensing water heater and used to determine a leakage in the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, the smart water valve 126 can determine that the temperature of the water leak of 60 degrees f matches the temperature of water consumed by the toilet of 177 degrees c (62 degrees f)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in some examples, the smart water valve 126 can determine that temperature of the water leak matches the temperature of the particular water consuming device based on the temperatures matching within a threshold variance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, although the present invention is equipped with a pressure sensor for detecting a hydraulic pressure drop occurring when a water pipe leaks, and an acoustic sensor for detecting a sound wave generated when a water pipe leaks, a compact arrangement is possible, and a sound / pressure composite sensor which prevents excessive increase of the temperature of the leaked water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, although the present invention is equipped with a pressure sensor for detecting a hydraulic pressure drop occurring when a water pipe leaks, and an acoustic sensor for detecting a sound wave generated when a water pipe leaks, a compact arrangement is possible, and a sound / pressure composite sensor which prevents excessive increase of the temperature of the leaked water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10508966-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the presence of the leak on the consumer side means that there is a constant flow of water from the water main through the external stop-tap and hence a constant heating effect and therefore the average temperature of the baseline is greater than compared to the first and second sites illustrated by figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this drop in temperature may mimic the thermal change caused by a leak in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate a leak signal when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate a leak signal when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate said leak condition when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate said leak condition when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected, marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected, marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the method may further include determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "either way as the user 102 performs temperature tests throughout the manifolds 112 and uses fixtures 122 selectively the user 102 can determine which pipelines 112 connect to the leaking pipe and have a leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "either way as the user 102 performs temperature tests throughout the manifolds 112 and uses fixtures 122 selectively the user 102 can determine which pipelines 112 connect to the leaking pipe and have a leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "so, after determining that the manifold 112 is before or after the leak 154, to determine which pipelines 114 are feedlines 116 or distribution lines 118, the user 102 has to perform another time temperature test with the fixture 122 turned on"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "so, after determining that the manifold 112 is before or after the leak 154, to determine which pipelines 114 are feedlines 116 or distribution lines 118, the user 102 has to perform another time temperature test with the fixture 122 turned on"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by performing time based temperature checks, the user 102 may determine that pipeline 114c has water flowing down towards the leak 154 at the main water entrance 108 to the property 104 and through pipeline 114c"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order for the user to determine where a distribution line 118 that has water flowing through the distribution line 118 to get to the leak 154 is going, the user 102 has to temperature check each pipeline 114a-114c of the manifold 112a and compare the results one by one with each fixture 122 present on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order for the user to determine where a distribution line 118 that has water flowing through the distribution line 118 to get to the leak 154 is going, the user 102 has to temperature check each pipeline 114a-114c of the manifold 112a and compare the results one by one with each fixture 122 present on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after opening up at these areas and performing temperature checks, the user 102 tries to determine 1) if the leak 154 is past or before said manifold 112 2) which one pipeline 114 is the feedline 116 and which pipeline(s) 114 are the distribution lines 118 and 3) which pipelines 114 in each manifold 112 take water to other fixtures 122 on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after opening up at these areas and performing temperature checks, the user 102 tries to determine 1) if the leak 154 is past or before said manifold 112 2) which one pipeline 114 is the feedline 116 and which pipeline(s) 114 are the distribution lines 118 and 3) which pipelines 114 in each manifold 112 take water to other fixtures 122 on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after performing this initial temperature test, the user 102 knows that pipeline 114c is a distribution line 118 and is most likely the pipeline 114 leading to the leak 154 because of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "11-18, because the hot water will be leaking out through the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 containing an underground leak 154 which will make the surrounding area around the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 and floors above the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 noticeably warmer via touch 142 or temperature testing equipment 144"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1612, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, the user 102 may safely assume and determine that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1714, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1814, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 126 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "moreover, the moisture and temperature sensors may not be positioned to detect a leak, for incipient freeze condition, and thus, the flow sensor would provide the last line of defense to water damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "moreover, the moisture and temperature sensors may not be positioned to detect a leak, for incipient freeze condition, and thus, the flow sensor would provide the last line of defense to water damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-6530263-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, prior art methods and apparati for detecting and locating a fluid leak in underground fluid conveying conduits typically fail to compensate for variances in the ambient temperature, thereby compromising the accuracy of the calculation of the location of the source of leaks in the pipeline, which is highly undesirable"}, {"pat_id": "US-6530263-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, prior art methods and apparati for detecting and locating a fluid leak in underground fluid conveying conduits typically fail to compensate for variances in the ambient temperature, thereby compromising the accuracy of the calculation of the location of the source of leaks in the pipeline, which is highly undesirable"}, {"pat_id": "US-7549435-B2", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "in such a configuration, a sensor, such as a temperature sensor, may be included to determine the source of a particular leak among one of a plurality of fluid sources"}, {"pat_id": "US-8403000-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "tank heat leak has a dramatic effect on the pressure temperature and density relationships of the lng thus making it very difficult to control the fuel tank pressure and maintain consistent fuel quality for delivery to the engine"}, {"pat_id": "US-8502687-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the determination module 302 determines the pipeline 100 works normally upon the condition that the fluid temperatures falls out of an allowable range or the leaks occur to the pipeline 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-9752787-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain pipe allows for any water that may build up in, or leak into, the valve box to drain away before it can change to steam under the high temperature conditions and cause damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-9752787-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain pipe allows for any water that may build up in, or leak into, the valve box to drain away before it can change to steam under the high temperature conditions and cause damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-9752787-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain pipe allows for any water that may build up in, or leak into, the valve box to drain away before it can change to steam under the high temperature conditions and cause damage"}]</data>
</edge>
