  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, the machine-learning algorithm can be trained with data provided from the control unit server 104, data provided by the smart water valve 126, and data associated with the security system 148 to predict devices that are leaking water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in response to providing the data from each of the devices in the monitored property 102 to the trained model, the trained model can produce a predicted device that is leaking based on the detection by the smart water valve 126"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "should the smart water valve produce a detection that water is leaking or the trained model predict a device that is leaking water in the monitored property 102, the control unit server 104 can provide that detection and/or prediction to the client device 122 of the property owner 120"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "similarly, the security system 148 can transmit a command to the smart water valve 126 to move the position of the ball valve 208 to open in response to the trained machine-learning model predicting no device is leaking water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "similarly, the security system 148 can transmit a command to the smart water valve 126 to move the position of the ball valve 208 to open in response to the trained machine-learning model predicting no device is leaking water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2599727-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the water leakage prevention device 1 is installed at the water leakage location, the drainage member 3 can be bypassed along the space where the existing equipment can be installed"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4029133-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "thereby, the rainwater drained from the lower connecting pipe can be guided to the inside of the gutter, and leakage from the connecting portion between the lower connecting pipe and the gutter can be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100736899-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if the ground connected to each other in the ground where the ground settlement is made, there is no relative position movement between the adjacent side openings, there is no leakage and excellent effect that can maintain the quality of the drain pipe excellent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101028522-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, since the natural water drainage is made smoothly by the leak prevention unit 20, there are advantages that the above-mentioned problems are solved at once"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this leakage path causes the drain and raw water to leave the fitting rather than entering the generated steam through the drain 320 shown in figures 3g-3i"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101730962-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this leakage path causes the drain and raw water to leave the fitting rather than entering the generated steam through the drain 320 shown in figures 3g-3i"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102009028-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "leakage drainage system for underground parking lot in apartment house waterproofing system for underground parking lot in apartment building the present invention relates to an underground parking lot leakage system drainage device for a multi-unit house, and more specifically, to provide a space for smoothly draining water in the underground parking lot, it is possible to keep the parking lot of the building clean through rapid drainage, it relates to a drainage system of the underground parking lot of the multi-unit house which can easily remove foreign substances filtered from the drainage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102009028-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, by providing a space for smoothly draining the water in the underground parking lot, it is possible to keep the parking lot of the building clean through rapid drainage, and leak in the underground parking lot of the apartment house that can easily remove foreign substances filtered out from the drainage system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102081866-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "this leakage path causes the effluent and raw water to leave the fit rather than enter the product vapor through the drain 320 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the algorithms can be trained to determine whether sensor data from a system is indicative of, for example, a normal activity (a normal flush), an abnormal activity (a minor, medium or major leak), a condition, and/or an activity in the fluid system"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is excessive local precipitation, the calculated susceptibility of water damage may be increased based on determining that the likelihood of water leaking into the property is much higher"}]</data>
