  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100633532-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in rainy weather with heavy rainfall, rainwater and sewage flowing through the rainwater and sewage inlets 23 of the manhole 10 increase, and the wear 40 formed inside the manhole 10 by the flow rate of the rainwater and sewage increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the water in the rainwater inlet space 12 filled with only clear rainwater may prevent contamination of the river even if it flows into the river through the rainwater discharge unit 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100779513-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the amount of rainwater flowing through the inlet 610 is large, as the main cartridge 620 and the auxiliary cartridge 630 are suspended, the extension part of the water gate 60 accommodated in the receiving groove 74 ( 64 is also moved upward to block the bottom discharge port 73 of the waterproof wall (70)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101089297-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the inner cylinder 142 is installed inside the inlet 122 to increase the flow rate of rainwater flowing into the contaminant collecting network 130, so that the contaminants mixed with rainwater (including the flocculents)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101218752-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the inlet part 21 may change the porosity and permeability coefficient according to the particle size of the aggregate used, and when the porosity and the permeability coefficient are increased, foreign matter may be included in the rainwater flowing into the collection pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is preferable that the area of the blocking plate 260 is made larger than the wastewater inlet 22 and the opening 110 to control the inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101261597-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the inflow of the fluid is small, all the fluid flowing into the second fluid inlet hole 22 can be introduced into the first fluid inlet hole 11 to go through the treatment process of contaminants, the fluid that does not flow into the first fluid inlet hole 11 may flow along the pipe to be drained to the drain pipe connector 23"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101353045-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second filter 400 is installed on the bottom surface of the filtration unit 3 of the housing 1 in a form surrounding the inlet of the outlet 20 to remove contaminants in the rainwater exiting through the outlet 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101375866-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, like the initial rainwater treatment device 100, the rainwater discharge reduction device 200 is a contaminant in the rainwater flowing through the rainwater inlet 250 and the rainwater inlet 250, the rainwater flows from the outside after filtering the filter may further include a filter net 260 to discharge the rainwater filtered to the vegetation filtration layer 210 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977695-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater on the road surface 1 flows through the inlet port 411 and falls to the upper side of the water permeable filter agent 493 to remove the contaminants adhering to the lower side of the screen net 492 and the water permeable filter agent 493 the drainage of the rainwater can be smoothly performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, especially in the rainy season or in the fall, foreign substances such as fallen leaves can block the inlet, making it difficult to drain, which can easily lead to flooding and human casualties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "flows in through the inlet (11), the rotation blocking plate (21) is pushed directly below the inlet (11) by the pressure or load generated, thereby allowing the inflow of sewage (1) or rainwater (2), etc., into the inlet (11)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when there is no inflow of sewage (1) or rainwater (2), etc., the rotation blocking plate (21) moves along the inclination angle (a) to be positioned directly below the inlet (11), thereby enabling the blocking of the foul odor (3)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338729-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention was devised to solve the above problem, and the sediment reduces the drop of sewage from the inlet of the sewer, thereby minimizing the lifting of the sediment, thereby reducing the amount of drainage that can prevent the sediment from entering the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200381089-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in case of rain, as the inflow of sewage increases, the frame plate is kept horizontal to block the sewage inlet"}]</data>
