  <data key="d6">["produce", "surround", "include", "transport", "get", "say", "occur", "freeze", "turn on", "base", "allow", "lead", "compare", "flow", "use", "contain", "increase", "cause", "prevent", "locate", "pipeline", "mark", "access", "determine", "block", "associate", "obtain", "affect", "leak out", "connect", "perform", "lift", "have", "form", "detect", "compromise", "serve", "examine", "convey", "check", "mimic", "try", "fight", "make", "substitute", "know", "assume", "designate", "compensate", "open up", "shut in", "spray", "go", "be", "leak", "fail", "fall"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-1086336-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by examining the temperature of the hydrocarbons along the length of the pipeline 10, an operator is able to increase the shut-in time to a point close to the critical time at which excessive deposits would have formed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 serves to prevent damage to the pipeline 510 due to volume expansion caused by freezing and freezing of the fire fighting water in the pipeline 510 due to the influence of low temperature in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "US-10537921-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "reference symbol 21 designates a filter unit, reference symbol 23 designates a temperature sensor, reference symbol 25 designates a level sensor, reference symbol 30 designates an object loading unit, reference symbol 31 designates a door lifting drive unit, reference symbol 33 designates a washing lifting drive unit, reference symbol 11 designates spray nozzles, reference symbol 13 designates spray pipelines, reference symbol 15 designates a manual valve, and reference symbol 17 designates electronic valves"}, {"pat_id": "US-10704740-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this drop in temperature may mimic the thermal change caused by a leak in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "at block 1806, the method includes affecting the temperature of the transported fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the promoting of heat transfer (block 1804) from the environment to the pipeline (e.g., when the external temperature is above a threshold) may increase the temperature of the fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11193847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in such embodiments, based on the sensor data determined by the temperature sensors 52, the control sub-system 54 may determine fluid temperature at multiple different locations along the bore in the pipeline system 10 (process block 106)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11199502-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is very easy to produce the natural gas hydrate in the oil and gas exploitation and transportation process especially in low-temperature and high-pressure deep water environments, and the natural gas hydrate will block a conveying pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12235188-B2", "para_id": "para_43", "text": "at the moment of leakage, the temperature of the inner surface of the thermal insulation layer 6 is the temperature of the outer wall of the pipeline without leakage, that is ton=tol, and thus, the variation of the transient heat capacity of steam at the moment of leakage can be obtained by substituting tol into the formula (1) \u03b4q"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected, marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature is detected, marking the particular floor associated with the noticeable increase in the temperature on the property as the area of the property to be used to access the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak for any future repair or replacement of the detectable underground cold water pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, the method may include checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the method may further include determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline containing the leak is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "either way as the user 102 performs temperature tests throughout the manifolds 112 and uses fixtures 122 selectively the user 102 can determine which pipelines 112 connect to the leaking pipe and have a leak 154"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "so, after determining that the manifold 112 is before or after the leak 154, to determine which pipelines 114 are feedlines 116 or distribution lines 118, the user 102 has to perform another time temperature test with the fixture 122 turned on"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by performing time based temperature checks, the user 102 may determine that pipeline 114c has water flowing down towards the leak 154 at the main water entrance 108 to the property 104 and through pipeline 114c"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order for the user to determine where a distribution line 118 that has water flowing through the distribution line 118 to get to the leak 154 is going, the user 102 has to temperature check each pipeline 114a-114c of the manifold 112a and compare the results one by one with each fixture 122 present on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after opening up at these areas and performing temperature checks, the user 102 tries to determine 1) if the leak 154 is past or before said manifold 112 2) which one pipeline 114 is the feedline 116 and which pipeline(s) 114 are the distribution lines 118 and 3) which pipelines 114 in each manifold 112 take water to other fixtures 122 on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after performing this initial temperature test, the user 102 knows that pipeline 114c is a distribution line 118 and is most likely the pipeline 114 leading to the leak 154 because of the temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "11-18, because the hot water will be leaking out through the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 containing an underground leak 154 which will make the surrounding area around the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 and floors above the underground leaking cold water pipeline 126 noticeably warmer via touch 142 or temperature testing equipment 144"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1612, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property is detected, the user 102 may safely assume and determine that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1712, after turning on the recirculation pump 180 and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines 114 in the first loop on the property 104 for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property 104 to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property 104"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1714, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 114 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1812, the method includes checking a temperature of all floors of the property 104 to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property 104 after turning on the pump 180 and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines 114 in the first loop on the property 104 for the period of time"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at step 1814, if the noticeable increase in the temperature of the particular floor anywhere on the property 104 is detected, the method includes determining that the detectable underground cold water pipeline 126 containing the leak 154 is located beneath or near the particular floor"}, {"pat_id": "US-6530263-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another example, prior art methods and apparati for detecting and locating a fluid leak in underground fluid conveying conduits typically fail to compensate for variances in the ambient temperature, thereby compromising the accuracy of the calculation of the location of the source of leaks in the pipeline, which is highly undesirable"}, {"pat_id": "US-8502687-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the determination module 302 determines the pipeline 100 works normally upon the condition that the fluid temperatures falls out of an allowable range or the leaks occur to the pipeline 100"}]</data>
</edge>
