  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the event that the rain overflow basin 1 is busy or there is a blockage in the area of the retaining element 8, the water can thus flow from the basin chamber 5 to the basin overflow 7 via the emergency overflow 16 without being cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2589989-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0016] the water retention block for a rainwater infiltration basin according to the invention is much lighter and easier to handle than a conventional water retention block, so that its volume can be increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715445-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the packing member interposed between the upper body and the rainwater collecting basin blocks the odor coming up from the sewer, thereby improving the living environment and preventing habitat for harmful insects such as flies and mosquitoes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating basin 230 is located side by side with the settling tank 210, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101367848-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the completion of the red soil and topographical cleanup process before the start of the fresh water supply process further includes a drainage tank installation process for forming a drainage basin at a predetermined interval by digging a pit of at least 3 6m deep on the red soil it is also possible in form"}]</data>
</edge>
