  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-1661864-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in the method (1) in which the surface oxidation layer is formed in the gas phase, a mixed gas of a nitrogen gas and a small amount of air is introduced into a reaction vessel at a low temperature to oxidize \u03b1-fe present in the surface of the iron particles, thereby obtaining iron composite particles having a surface oxidation layer composed of fe3o4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101611632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the sub-chambers of the vessel 12, additional water vapor is produced and the temperature of the water vapor is raised to leave salt, dissolved solids, and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828136-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the lower chambers of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased to produce additional water vapor, leaving salts, dissolved solids and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659347-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the method according to my invention comprises the steps of (a) emitting the water in one or more jets into a vessel maintained under a pressure low enough to let part of that water be vaporized--together with accompanying contaminants--at an ambient temperature, preferably at or below the usual room temperature of about 20 -25 c."}, {"pat_id": "US-5100560-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this oxidation method, the waste material is pressurized and fed into a reactor vessel along with compressed oxidant, either oxygen, air or oxygen-enriched air, and maintained therein under supercritical temperature conditions, that is at a temperature above 374 c., and, elevated pressure, to cause rapid oxidation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5100560-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in any case, the rotation of the blade means 60 will cause the blade members 62 to pass along the interior wall 12 of the vessel 10 dislodging any accumulated deposits which then fall into the brine slurry in the subcritical temperature zone 16 in the bottom of the vessel 10 wherein the solids will dissolve in the cold brine fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-8556998-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the treatment was conducted for an hour with the pressure, temperature and shearing force inside the vessel kept at the aforesaid values to remove the water from the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "US-8556998-B2", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the treatment was conducted for an hour with the pressure, temperature and shearing force inside the vessel kept at the aforesaid values, to remove the water from the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "US-9102545-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the water and water vapor passes through each subchamber of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased such that additional water vapor is created and leaves the salts, dissolved solids, and other contaminants behind in the remaining water"}]</data>
</edge>
