  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-2410094-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a partition tank has been formed capable of mounting a rainwater collecting surface thereon which offers good resistance to deformation by the tubular shape of these tubes"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3577440-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first invention comprises a storage tank or water storage tank section 2, an upper water-shielding sheet section 3, and a rainwater discharging and cooling device section 4, and is configured to remove rainwater, snowmelt water, and the like accumulated on the upper surface of the upper water-shielding sheet section 3"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5349271-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "thus, if the water penetration hole 40h is provided in the wing-shaped vertical wall 40w of the vertical block 40, rainwater can flow through the water penetration hole 40h, so that the rainwater enters the water storage tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5388757-B2", "para_id": "para_39", "text": "in this case, the amount of rainwater in the tank main body 2 can be confirmed in advance by the measuring tube 18 by the above-described method, thereby avoiding inconveniences such as unexpected water breakage in the middle of watering and performing good watering"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention is installed in the basement penetration type, first digging a pit having a certain width and depth, and then flatten the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100485742-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, when the rainwater stored in the rainwater storage tank is drained underground through the drain hole 3a formed in the slab 3, the earth and sand can be prevented from entering the rainwater storage tank together with the rainwater by the nonwoven fabric 23 laid in the pit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531031-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100660052-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because of this, the block body 30 is installed in a row arrangement of the role of the storage tank for storing rainwater and the waterway line is formed so that the concentrated phenomenon does not occur even in a large amount of rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927631-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when rainwater flows into the sedimentation tank 200, heavy foreign matter such as sand sinks to the bottom and light foreign matter such as leaves or vinyl fragments rises on the surface of the water to easily remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952605-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the volume of the body block and the storage block having a hexahedron shape increases and the weight thereof increases, it is very cumbersome and inconvenient to assemble the rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, particulate contaminants contained in rainwater fall into the sediment holding tank 410 and is confined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101101703-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "according to the present invention, it is possible to effectively purify the rainwater having a high degree of contamination, and to variably mount the biostone storage means by the rack and the rack support frame, thereby simplifying the installation and removal in the filtration tank and the long-term rainwater filtration"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the tip of the connecting pipe 50 is bent downward so as to be submerged in the rainwater in the sedimentation tank 10, contaminants having a small specific gravity such as oil floating on the water surface may not pass through the connecting pipe 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the manager removes the grating 23 to open the rain gutter 22 and connects the collecting rod to the lifting hook 27a on the ground, the container 27 is lifted to the outside of the rainwater storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101183691-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the rainwater storage tank of this patent is a large weighted product, and as the size and volume of the unit body block itself increases, the construction work of the rainwater storage tank has to be corrected by a crane if it is not correctly placed at the construction position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101219791-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1, non-contaminant purification device characterized in that it further comprises a filtration tank connected to the rain pipe and the rainwater flowing through the flow passage of the rain pipe flows to remove foreign substances piggybacked in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101226126-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, unlike the conventional state that could not be artificially checked the internal condition, the rainwater storage tank according to the present invention has the effect that it is possible to properly clean and remove the floating matter by checking the state of the interior even after construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101238199-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as such, rainwater storage tanks at home and abroad are often installed in excess of 2m, which is the design depth of the first-class bridges, and the excess weight may cause not only deformation of the storage tank but also collapse"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101238199-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as such, rainwater storage tanks at home and abroad are often installed in excess of 2m, which is the design depth of the first-class bridges, and the excess weight may cause not only deformation of the storage tank but also collapse"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in this case, between the wall blocks 200 continuously arranged in the transverse direction to form the wall surface of the rainwater storage tank, the engaging portion of the recess portion 210 and the convex portion 220 is formed, and thus the strand wire 10 and the strand wire installation tool ( 100), the fastener 50, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process, and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water, thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, rainwater and contaminants from the side of the road 1 flow together through these steel gratings 102 and 104 and are then stored in the settling tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating paper 130 is positioned side by side with the settling tank 110, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating basin 230 is located side by side with the settling tank 210, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101358438-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 50 is supplied with rainwater from which sand and oil have been removed from the sedimentation tank 40, and various foreign matters contained in the rainwater [such as foreign matters of fine particles, etc., which are not sorted in the contaminant separator 20 and the sedimentation tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in detail, the purification treatment tank 10 removes the fine turbidity contaminants or soluble contaminants contained in the rainwater passing through the precipitation tank 20 and the precipitation tank 20 removing the floating contaminants and the suspended solids from the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101817003-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "next, the rainwater that has been purified through the water purification apparatus 2 is moved to the storage tank 3 along the connection line 52, thereby enabling a large amount of water to be supplied as moisture necessary for growing the water loss water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101857595-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since the blocks used in the rainwater storage tank are usually manufactured as a separate product to meet the construction site, it is difficult to produce standardized blocks, and in order to use blocks smaller or larger than the manufactured blocks, there is a problem that falls significantly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102005372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even when the fixed mesh filter 110 is blocked, an appropriate amount of rainwater should be introduced into the float removing tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to provide a rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank that is easy to clean the removed contaminants separately"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank that can effectively remove contaminants contained in the rainwater in the process of collecting rainwater, and easy to clean the removed contaminants separately"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102095891-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "another object of the present invention is to remove the non-point contaminants by passing the initial rainwater through a rainwater bypass (\u96e8\u6c34 \u96e8) and bypassing the rainwater filtered through the screen of the pretreatment tank equipped with a screen through a downward filtration in a filtering tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, it was configured to block rainwater flowing into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40, so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if a rainwater blocking tent (60) and frame (61) are not installed in the car wash section (10) of the car wash, there is an effect of resolving the problem of overload caused by rainwater flowing into the wastewater storage tank (30)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "road drainage with first flush treatment ability the present invention is to insert a filter filling tank having a filtration treatment function in the conventional rainwater receiver to the road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function that can reliably remove and treat contaminants contained in the road surface drainage"}]</data>
