  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3672455-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, since the activity of iron bacteria, that is, the oxidation amount of iron may change due to the influence of temperature, the measuring tank 10 is maintained at a temperature at which the activity of iron bacteria is stabilized by the temperature regulator 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "under the control of the drive means and the control means, the temperature of the cold water tank is raised to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention has been made to solve the above problems, an object of the present invention is to determine the freezing of the cold water tank according to the changing product internal temperature and cold water temperature to determine the freezing of the cold water tank even in the winter at low room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "four-way valve driving means for driving control of the four-way valve to prevent freezing of the cold water tank, it is characterized in that the compressor driving means for controlling the drive to increase the temperature of the cold water tank according to the control to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is determined whether or not the preset ice generating temperature tcd (cold water temperature at which freezing occurs in the cold water tank)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the temperature control apparatus and the method of the cold / hot water purifier according to the present invention as described above, it is determined whether the cold water tank is freezing according to the changing product internal temperature and the cold water temperature, so that the cold water tank freezes even in the winter when the room temperature is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100953075-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, latent heat is scattered with water vapor during the dropping to evaporate the organic oxidation heat and the denitrification heat, and the temperature of the microorganism activity of the oxidizing tank is changed to the atmospheric temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194148-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the temperature is lowered, the outdoor temperature may not directly affect the water tank, thus delaying the freezing time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101240216-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aerobic digestion tank 100 in which organic matter contained in waste water is oxidatively decomposed by activation of high temperature aerobic microorganisms, and an air nozzle provided at an inner lower portion of the aerobic digestion tank 100 to discharge air providing a lifting force for circulating the waste water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101265963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "comprising an apparatus for maintaining a reaction temperature in an aerobic tank, and forming an optimum reaction condition in the aerobic tank even with an external temperature change, thereby improving the efficiency of organic matter oxidation and nitrification and thereby stable discharge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the first cover 20 and the second cover 30 is provided to cover the opening of the water tank 10 to prevent the inflow of foreign matter and infiltration of bacteria in the air, the first cover 20 the space between the second cover 30 serves as a thermal insulation space to block the influence of the external temperature of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, the first cover 200 covers the opening of the water tank 100 to prevent the inflow of foreign substances and the penetration of bacteria in the air, and the space between the first cover 200 and the second cover 300 is it functions as an insulated space to block the influence of the outside temperature of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101642081-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, even when only the oxidizing agent is supplied to the regeneration wastewater purification tank 140 during purification of regeneration wastewater, on the other hand, if the temperature of the regeneration wastewater is lower than the reference temperature, the oxidizing efficiency of the oxidizing agent is lowered, so that it is required to supply the reaction catalyst for promoting the oxidation reaction in addition to the oxidizing agent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in the above-described embodiment, although the water treatment system has determined to perform the chemical cleaning when the contamination index of the membrane filtration tank is equal to or greater than the second value, in another embodiment, the chemical washing is performed according to at least one of the temperature, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101861072-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the thermal hydrolysis apparatus 65 is operated to remove the concentrated sludge from the sludge concentration tank 60 under conditions of high temperature (about 150 c) and high pressure (about 20 bar) to methane fermentation of the post-"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "after checking only the temperature of the water inside the water tank (1) to determine the operation of the heater member 20 as the temperature inside the water tank (1) or less than 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "thus, when the temperature of the storage tank 100 is below a certain temperature, the freezing prevention function operates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the contrary, in the case where the mlss concentration is increased, the wastewater temperature in the tank is maintained at about 30 to 40 c during the biological treatment in the liquid corrosion tank, which is caused by the difference between the external temperature and the air supplied into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti-freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process (aop)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti-freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process (aop)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102883227-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a wastewater storage facility where wastewater containing ammonia is stored, a cavitation generating device that receives wastewater discharged from the above wastewater storage tank and generates cavitation to increase the temperature of wastewater containing ammonia"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-2004