p of determining the number of water to be confirmed for a certain time, and if a predetermined number or more is confirmed, drainage of the water tank and opening the valve and draining the water, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, checking the water level when the water level is confirmed, and draining the water by opening the water drain valve of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120, even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase, the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101033272-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the fish tank 300 is increased and the flow rate supplied to the cleaner through the drain port 301 increases, the flow rate may be reduced by lifting the cleaner, and the water level of the fish tank 300 is lowered so that the drain port 301 may be reduced"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sludge storage tank 100 increases above a predetermined level, the flow rate controller 110 increases the output of the transfer pump 107 to increase the flow amount of sludge transferred to the cavitation storage tank 120, and the sludge storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the water level of the sludge storage tank 100 is 100 to 120% of the set water level, since the water level becomes the full water level, four cavitation generators 130 corresponding to four levels can be operated to greatly increase the throughput of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention by installing the filtration device 200 in the position as described above, the contaminants in the water discharged through the drain pipe 120 from the swimming pool to be filtered immediately before passing through the water level control tank (300)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, when the purified treatment water from which the contaminants have been removed through the purification treatment water recovery pipe 140 provided in the internal treatment tank 200 of the present invention is recovered, the amount corresponding to the purification treatment water by the water level detection means and the control unit 600"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101383594-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and according to the variable level screen filter according to the present invention, it is possible to support the variable screen unit in connection with the water tank to improve the durability of the equipment, the deformation of the variable screen unit according to the water level is made more quickly to increase the treatment efficiency of sewage it can be effective"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sewage stored in the tank 30 rises and the height of the buckle member 54 increases, the wire 56b is pulled up by the load of the sensing block 56c and the sensing block 56c is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101660087-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the amount of the treated water w introduced into the treated water storage tank 50 gradually increases during the electrolysis step s30, the water level of the treated water w gradually increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676999-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, according to the present invention, it is possible to monitor the state of water leakage or foreign matter introduced into the water tank 1 by monitoring the rapid change of the water level and the water quality, thereby enabling cleaner and safer water quality management"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a control unit for controlling driving of the pressurization pressurizing pump to transport the contaminated water to the land storage tank when the internal water level of the shielding facility is higher than a predetermined reference value, and the inside water level of the shielding facility can be adjusted by being transported in both directions between the storage tank and the polluted water storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the present invention, a pipeline is installed between the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant and the land storage tank, and the polluted water of the shielding facility is transported to the land storage tank by the pipeline, thereby reducing the water level in the shielding facility of the marine waste treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit 180 controls the driving of the pressurization pressurizing pump 170 to bypass the contaminated water to the land storage tank 140 when the internal water level of the shielding facility 110 is higher than a predetermined reference value"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in the case of the domestic west coast, the polluted water is transported to the land-based storage tank 140 through the polluted water storage tank 130, thereby indicating that the internal water level of the shielding facility 110 can be lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102391446-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "specifically, the control device 30 may determine whether filter cleaning is necessary by checking whether the water level in the water tank is equal to or greater than a preset threshold value based on the water level detection information"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102400040-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the water level of the treated water tank is measured in real time, and when the water level is out of a certain range, the gate valve is selectively opened and closed to block the flow path of the overflow pipe, thereby increasing the overflow height of the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102554668-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "will leak control unit 112 is configured to cause ro pump 450 to stop pumping if empty level switch 350a in tank 350 detects air or a critically low water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102879590-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and a batch type wastewater treatment system characterized by including a control unit that controls the rectifier lifting unit according to the signal of the sensor, thereby raising the rectifier in conjunction with the rise in the water level of the reaction tank when wastewater flows in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102903436-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "is opened by the bending deformation of the elastic membrane (95), so that the amount of polluted air input through the horizontal passage (14) increases, and when the water level in the water tank (91)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102903436-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "is opened by the bending deformation of the elastic membrane (95), so that the amount of polluted air introduced through the horizontal channel (14) increases, and when the water level in the water tank (91)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200332116-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when the water tank level is a high water level, the flow of water is blocked by the float 42 and the pressure valve 43, so that the current of the pump motor increases without being stabilized as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365446-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by using the control equipment, the water level difference between the upper and the downstream filtration tanks is maintained at 1.0-1.5m, so that the sediment deposited in the upper and the downstream filtration tanks can be gradually discharged during the initial flooding with less floating dust, thereby preventing the ultimate closure of the filter media"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is to maintain a constant water level using a float valve and to supply a constant concentration of brine to the electrolysis tank so that sodium hypochlorite is equipped with an automatic valve and a flow sensor to produce a constant concentration of sodium hypochlorite it is to provide a generator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, by maintaining the water level at all times using the float valve 131, the suction pressure of saturated brine can be kept constant, and a constant concentration of salt water can be supplied to the electrolysis tank to produce sodium hypochlorite of a constant concentration"}, {"pat_id": "US-4709723-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "during periods of high ground water levels, this leakage enabled additional fluid to flow into the tank to compensate for the increased hydraulic pressure of surrounding ground water and water saturated soil"}, {"pat_id": "US-6627073-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the water level in the area on the uppermost stream side in the electrolytic tank is controlled in a predetermined range, as in the claim 16, therefore, it is possible to more reliably prevent the water from leaking from the electrolytic tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-9352978-B2", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "should the flow of water into the feed tank 46 and into the treatment container 48 become so great that the pumps 92 are overwhelmed, or should electrical power to the pumps 92 be interrupted and water level overflow the space 102 and rise high enough, the overflow pipe 56 can carry a portion of the excess water to the intermediate collection container 28, which can act as a buffer at least temporarily"}]</data>
