  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-3883596-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in order to use the contact material 4 as a filter medium, the porosity of the contact material 4 must be 90% or more, like the contact material 3 provided in the precipitation tank 1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315874-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1b, is a modification of the a 2 / o method to increase the removal efficiency of phosphorus and nitrogen, wastewater through the first settling tank 100 anaerobic reactor 200, the first anoxic reactor 300, the first aerobic oxidation tank 400, the second anoxic reactor 500, the second aerobic reactor 600 and the second precipitation tank 700, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100341208-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, the sludge produced by solidification and precipitation in step s2 is applied to the concentration tank to remove the water primarily to form a filter cake (step s6), the filter cake formed in step s6 is finally removed by the water discharged (step s7)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100403183-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "a highly concentrated precipitation tank for filtration, oxidation, and decomposition to remove biochemical oxygen demand (bod) and suspended solids (ss)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100440250-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after adjusting the ph, the oxidation reaction is carried out in the reactor, and then, the precipitate is adjusted by adjusting the appropriate ph in the precipitation tank for aggregation and precipitation, and then neutralized so as not to affect the microbial growth"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442932-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "the secondary treatment water in which the solid matter is removed by switching to the secondary precipitation tank 12b is sent to the oxidation tank 22, and the sludge precipitated in the secondary precipitation tank 12b is for the primary sludge treatment tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100442933-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the precipitation in the settling tank (l2a, b) to the decoloration treatment by the electrolytic oxidation treatment and untreated to remove the organic pollutants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and converting the heavy metal into a corrosion precursor which is insoluble in water by a biological corrosion reaction, and sends it to the primary precipitation tank (5a) to precipitate and remove the solid material, and then to the primary treatment tank (13), and then to the primary precipitation tank (5a)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in the primary aeration tank (3a), when organic pollutants and heavy metals in the waste water are converted into corrosion precursors that are insoluble in water by biological corrosion reactions, they are sent to the primary precipitation tank (5a) to remove the corrosion precursors and microorganisms that exist in the solid state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100449379-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "after the oxidation treatment, it is sent to the reaction tank 18 to supply the emulsion resin and the flocculant to solidify the unremoved heavy metal component, and then to stir slowly by the flocculation tank stirrer 21 to facilitate precipitation or pressure flotation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100605267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the waste water passing through the bypass pipe 20 is treated water that does not pass only the filtration tank 17, and is discharged through precipitation in the apparatus, so that almost contaminants are removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100706536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the agglomeration tank and the belt press may be further mounted between the ozone treatment tank and the ultraviolet treatment tank, thereby further improving the filtration efficiency by further performing the removal of agglomerates through oxidation and precipitation and aggregation by the oxidant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an electrolysis device installed in the aerobic iron precipitation tank, the electrolysis module having an electrode mounted thereon, and an insoluble precipitate precipitated by reaction of an oxide produced by electrolysis of the electrolysis module and phosphate contained in the mixed solution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the organic material and phosphorus are removed by the oxygen-free tank 40, the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50, and the electrolysis device 60, and nitrogen is removed in the nitrification and denitrification"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50 removes organic substances by metabolic activity of microorganisms, oxidizes ammonia nitrogen and nitrite nitrogen to nitrate nitrogen by oxygen supplied through a blower, and causes electrolysis of iron or aluminum electrodes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101019590-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2, the aging reaction of the oxide of the aeration oxidation water oxidized in the aeration tank 100, and precipitates the precipitate produced it is preferable that a reaction precipitation tank 200 for performing the precipitation step is provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101050144-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, biological treatment apparatus for sewage and wastewater, which is widely used at present, is provided with an aeration tank, which is an organic oxidation tank, and a precipitation tank for precipitating microorganisms grown in the aeration tank, thereby oxidizing and removing organic matter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365215-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the photocatalytic oxidation tank 190 sterilizes, disinfects and removes contaminants through the photocatalytic reaction of uv-tio 2 from the treated water separated and discharged from the precipitation tanks 142 and 160"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365215-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the photocatalytic oxidation tank 190 sterilizes, disinfects and removes contaminants through the photocatalytic reaction of uv-tio 2 from the treated water separated and discharged from the precipitation tanks 142 and 160"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in detail, the purification treatment tank 10 removes the fine turbidity contaminants or soluble contaminants contained in the rainwater passing through the precipitation tank 20 and the precipitation tank 20 removing the floating contaminants and the suspended solids from the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101580859-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "[ therefore, the gravity type precipitation in the pretreatment tank and the primary treatment water in which the sediment and the contaminants are removed by the trapping net 110 are flowed to the filtration treatment tank 20 through the primary treatment water inflow pipe 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101868534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the electrolytic waste liquid and the precipitating accelerator are not mixed uniformly, and the undrawn salt from the supernatant of the precipitation tank can be removed from the electrodeposition / adsorption unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102048511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the sludge is removed through the modular inclined member 770 and the purified water is discharged through the overflow wear 711 formed on each edge of the sedimentation tank 710 of the precipitation facility 700, the the water discharged through the overflowware 711 is discharged through the discharge tank 750"}, {"pat_id": "US-10696574-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in step (1), after the oxidation reaction and the precipitation reaction, the precipitation can be removed by any suitable method in the art, such as filtering, and the employed filtering apparatus can be any filtering apparatus known in the art, preferably sedimentation tank, sand filter, multi-media filter, etc"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659463-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this system thus allows the sulphur to oxidize and precipitate in the aeration/precipitation tank and the iron to continue its oxidation and precipitation in such aeration/precipitation tank"}]</data>
</edge>
