  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-4377451-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in such an aerobic sewage purification apparatus, in particular, when an abnormality occurs in the blower, the inside of the septic tank cannot be maintained in a normal aerobic condition, the purification function is lowered, and untreated water from the septic tank to the river is discharged and becomes environmental pollution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100299334-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the reverse contact oxidation method, a water barrier is formed in the middle of the river to introduce the river water into the primary storage tank, and when the rainfall increases, the river is discharged to discharge the river water to protect the river water purification device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100352584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the present invention is to solve the above problems to provide an apparatus that effectively removes the algae and contaminants generated in lakes, rivers and the ocean in-site (no site) without the need for a separate treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100352584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the present invention can effectively remove algae and contaminants generated in lakes, rivers, and the sea, etc., in site without the need for a separate treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the general water purification apparatus by the catalytic oxidation method includes a primary storage tank that collects contaminated river water with various wastewater discharged from a home, a factory, or a non-point source, and removes sludge that is settled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100399294-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the screen tank 110 is used to separate the large contaminants contained in the sewage when living sewage flows into the river, the screen tank 110, according to the size of the contaminants and the fine screen (article 75mm, detail 10mm) to remove the impurities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, after treating the roadbed sediment and sediment contaminants contained in the sewage of rainy weather has been developed and used to flow into natural rivers or nearby sea, there is a storage tank type treatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102451025-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, if the sediment deposited on the bottom of the storage tank is not removed through washing in a timely manner, decay and severe odors are generated, as well as sediment from the influent flows into the river or river"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the river water to be treated, which has passed through the pretreatment unit (10), flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit (30), is purified in the biological contact oxidation treatment unit (30), and then passes through the discharge tank (40) to be discharged into a river or lake, thereby performing the functions of water quality purification and management during normal times"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stromwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stromwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stromwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stormwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stormwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stormwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}]</data>
