aminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the contaminants accumulated on the bottom surface of the sediment holding tank 410 may be prevented from rising to the filter plate accommodating part 160 by riding the drain pipe 420"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, particulate contaminants contained in rainwater fall into the sediment holding tank 410 and is confined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985170-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the tip of the connecting pipe 50 is bent downward so as to be submerged in the rainwater in the sedimentation tank 10, contaminants having a small specific gravity such as oil floating on the water surface may not pass through the connecting pipe 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the manager removes the grating 23 to open the rain gutter 22 and connects the collecting rod to the lifting hook 27a on the ground, the container 27 is lifted to the outside of the rainwater storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, after treating the roadbed sediment and sediment contaminants contained in the sewage of rainy weather has been developed and used to flow into natural rivers or nearby sea, there is a storage tank type treatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101191166-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the ground can support the side plate block, the side pressure of the rain water temporarily stored in the storage tank need not be taken into consideration when installing the side plate block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101219791-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1, non-contaminant purification device characterized in that it further comprises a filtration tank connected to the rain pipe and the rainwater flowing through the flow passage of the rain pipe flows to remove foreign substances piggybacked in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in this case, between the wall blocks 200 continuously arranged in the transverse direction to form the wall surface of the rainwater storage tank, the engaging portion of the recess portion 210 and the convex portion 220 is formed, and thus the strand wire 10 and the strand wire installation tool ( 100), the fastener 50, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process, and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water, thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwat