  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, between the second compartment member 400 and the storm water receiving tank 100 is further provided with a contaminant filtration adsorption means 700 filled with a filter medium to remove the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the organic integrity of the floor block, corner wall block, side wall block, column block, ceiling border block, and ceiling block strengthens the overall integrity of the storm storage tank, thereby ensuring structural stability of the storm storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391172-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a filtration tank for removing fine contaminants in the initial storm that have passed through the swirl screen and discharging the initial storm in the state where fine contaminants have been removed through the discharge pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 210 is also provided with a filter means 220 for purifying the effluent from which solids contained in the storm and fine contaminants are removed from the stormwater inflow pipe 140 of the storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the inlet tank 100 is formed with a screen box 120 to remove contaminants from the storm water discharged from the inlet pipe 110 and is formed at a lower side of the screen box 120, the desulphurization tool 130 is formed to have a flow regulating function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101859056-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "therefore, the storage tank structure for stormwater infiltration and storage according to the present invention can ensure sufficient durability against repetitive vehicle shafts since the storage unit blocks have sufficient strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of t