acteristic tolerances"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, this process may continue for as many treatment blocks 260 as there are in the treatment system 200, until a final permeate stream, optionally having untreated filtered seawater water blended therein, is produced from a final membrane pressure vessel"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, this process may continue for as many treatment blocks 260 as there are in the treatment system 200, until a final permeate stream, optionally having untreated filtered seawater water blended therein, is produced from a final membrane pressure vessel"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4a-b, the filtered seawater may be provided to a treatment block 260 and either sent through blend/bypass line 225 or pumped by variable speed high-pressure pump 212, which pushes the filtered seawater through to one or more membrane pressure vessels (e.g., 214, 216, and 218), thereby creating a permeate stream and a concentrate stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4a-b, the filtered seawater may be provided to a treatment block 260 and either sent through blend/bypass line 225 or pumped by variable speed high-pressure pump 212, which pushes the filtered seawater through to one or more membrane pressure vessels (e.g., 214, 216, and 218), thereby creating a permeate stream and a concentrate stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4a-b, the filtered seawater may be provided to a treatment block 260 and either sent through blend/bypass line 225 or pumped by variable speed high-pressure pump 212, which pushes the filtered seawater through to one or more membrane pressure vessels (e.g., 214, 216, and 218), thereby creating a permeate stream and a concentrate stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4a-b, the filtered seawater may be provided to a treatment block 260 and either sent through blend/bypass line 225 or pumped by variable speed high-pressure pump 212, which pushes the filtered seawater through to one or more membrane pressure vessels (e.g., 214, 216, and 218), thereby creating a permeate stream and a concentrate stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6a-b, a system and/or method of the present invention may be configured so that the variable speed high-pressure pump 212 pushes the filtered seawater 611 through one or more treatment blocks, thereby creating a concentrate stream 634 and a permeate stream (not shown)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if, in block 8016, the system 6000 is not in a production start-up state, in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, in block 8016, the system 6000 is not in a production start-up state, in block 8020 the target temperature for the blowdown process stream exiting the blowdown heat exchanger 6008b may be set to the desired temperature determined in block 8014"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the forwardly directed stream from the nozzle 19 is particularly useful in creating an initial opening through a blockage caused by most materials"}, {"pat_id": "US-5988188-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, plugs may be positioned both upstream of the nozzle and downstream of the obstruction for blocking flow from upstream in the sewer line and creating a flow restriction downstream of the obstruction"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "detecting by the strain gauge the presence of any strain changes in the pipeline at the selected position caused by the pressure changes and determining therefrom whether the blockage is upstream or downstream of the selected position"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "detecting by the strain gauge the presence of any strain changes in the pipeline at the selected position caused by the pressure changes and determining therefrom whether the blockage is upstream or downstream of the selected position"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by using very sensitive but readily available bonded resistance strain gauges , it can determine if there are pressure changes in the pipeline, thereby indicating whether there is blockage upstream or downstream of the test site"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by using very sensitive but readily available bonded resistance strain gauges , it can determine if there are pressure changes in the pipeline, thereby indicating whether there is blockage upstream or downstream of the test site"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "once the direction of the blockage has been ascertained, that is whether the strain gauge is upstream or downstream of the blockage, the gauge can be removed from the outside of the pipeline and the pipeline s external coating repaired (if necessary)"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "once the direction of the blockage has been ascertained, that is whether the strain gauge is upstream or downstream of the blockage, the gauge can be removed from the outside of the pipeline and the pipeline s external coating repaired (if necessary)"}, {"pat_id": "US-6725717-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "pressures in the pipeline on an upstream side 9 of the blockage can be increased or lowered but do not readily transmit or do not transmit at all to the down stream side 12 of the blockage"}]</data>
