  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101255061-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "receiving temperature information of the water flowing through the water pipe from the smart water meter, receiving outdoor temperature information from the meteorological server, and determining whether a water meter is in danger of freezing in accordance with the temperature information of the water in the water pipes and the outside temperature information, if the water meter determines that there is a risk of freezing waves, it provides a freeze prevention system of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101255061-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "is provided with outdoor temperature information from the water pipes, and judges whether the water meter is in danger of freezing in accordance with the water temperature information of the water pipes and the outside temperature information, and if it is determined that the water meter is in danger of freezing, to the user wire / wireless terminal of the water meter it provides a management server, characterized in that to send a freezing warning"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101423708-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10-0926266.the present invention relates to a water meter which is capable of reducing the expansion pressure caused by the freezing of the interior of a winter casing having a low temperature in a prior art water meter, thereby remarkably decreasing the functionality and durability of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101542382-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "10-2004-0013366 (published on february 14, 2004) in embodiments of the present invention, tap water flows automatically so that the water meter can not be frozen when the water reaches a temperature at which the water inside the water meter can be frozen even if the user does not use tap water, thereby preventing freezing of the water meter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2 is an operation diagram showing a color change according to a temperature change of the freezing wave prediction temperature sheet 150 in the water meter 100 equipped with a freezing temperature prediction sheet according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the water meter 100 provided with the freezing wave prediction sheet according to an embodiment of the present invention, the freezing wave prediction temperature sheet 150 has a second set temperature (eg, -5 degrees) that is lower than the first set temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the water meter 100 equipped with the freezing wave prediction sheet according to an embodiment of the present invention, the freezing wave prediction temperature sheet 150 has a first color at a first set temperature (for example, 0 degrees celsius) or more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to detect a color change based on the temperature of tap water, it is provided (strictly attached) to the outer shell 110 of the water meter 100, and the freezing prediction temperature sheet 150 includes the water meter 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102116121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the water meter 100 equipped with a freezing sheet for predicting a freezing wave according to an embodiment of the present invention, the second zion region 152 is equal to or less than a second set temperature (eg, -5 degrees c)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102158188-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4 is an operation diagram showing a color change according to a temperature change of the freezing wave prediction zion sheet 150 in the freezing wave prediction water meter system according to an embodiment of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102158188-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the freeze prediction sheet 150 is characterized in that the color changes according to the temperature of the outside air in which the water meter 100 is installed, so that the user can directly check the possibility of freezing of the water meter 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102158188-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the freezing wave prediction water meter system according to an embodiment of the present invention, the freezing wave prediction zion sheet 150 is a water meter 100 in order to change color based on the temperature of tap water passing through the fluid passage hole 111"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102158188-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "7, in the freezing wave prediction water meter system according to an embodiment of the present invention, the freezing wave prediction zion sheet 150 is color based on the temperature of the tap water passing through the fluid passage hole 111"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102466363-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, when the outside temperature drops below freezing, such as in winter, the water flowing inside the main body of the water meter freezes and expands, and the expansion force may cause a freeze phenomenon that damages the glass cover of the meter or damages the meter itself"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200387639-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, warm geothermal heat is introduced in the winter season, so that the temperature inside the water meter protector can maintain a temperature similar to that of the geothermal temperature, thereby preventing freezing of water meters and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200415979-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, since water meters installed in buildings such as apartment complexes are installed in corridors that are not heated, they are easily influenced by temperature and are easily frozen when the temperature drops sharply, thus exposing more of them to the risk of freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200487219-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this water meter 10, tap water is allowed to pass through the water meter, so that when the air temperature falls below freezing in winter, tap water passing through the water meter is frozen, and thus the water meter 10 is frequently frozen"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}]</data>
</edge>
